ve money sort of  considerations there's a lot of stuff  where we need more money in the short  term like infrastructure upgrading  buildings switching federal buildings to  renewable energy etc etc we're in the  short term we actually have to spend  more over the long term we will save the  problem with these conversations about  what to cut is that once you understand  you you can't how do I want to say this  everything is a negotiation  there's tons of favors and amendments  and this is sort of like how policy is  done right now and to really cut  properly to have a shot at actually  cutting the types of spending that is  the problematic spending you need to  completely change so many aspects of our  political system and there's a lot of  good books written about this and  articles about it but you know me  listing stuff maybe is interesting and I  don't think I'd have anything super  surprising but what we need to actually  change is the way that this system of  cronyism and oh you know wink wink I'll  go for your amendment if you go for mine  and this port  you know everybody's put that the truth  is we talk about pork barrel projects  everybody's poor you know everybody's  pork is someone else's in many cases  community project right so you know I  get you to sign off on rebuilding some  ice rinks in my district and that seems  like pork if you're representing Hawaii  and I'm in Illinois but then you reverse  it and we have very similar situations  looking from Illinois over to Hawaii and  this is really part of the problem and  part of the problem of how budgeting is  done but all of that being said  Department of Defense military  absolutely huge opportunities to cut for  sure no question about it okay make sure  that you don't miss today's bonus show  which will be hosted by producer Pat you  can get instant access by becoming a  member at join pakman.com or a patron at  patreon.com slash david pakman show we  will be back on Monday later next week  we will